{
  "an6.44:0.1": "Numbered Discourses 6.44 ",
  "an6.44:0.2": "5. About Dhammika ",
  "an6.44:0.3": "With Migasālā ",
  "an6.44:1.1": "Then Venerable Ānanda robed up in the morning and, taking his bowl and robe, went to the home of the laywoman Migasālā, where he sat down on the seat spread out. ",
  "an6.44:1.2": "Then the laywoman Migasālā went up to Ānanda, bowed, sat down to one side, and said to him, ",
  "an6.44:2.1": "“Honorable Ānanda, how on earth are we supposed to understand the teaching taught by the Buddha, when the chaste and the unchaste are both reborn in exactly the same place in the next life? ",
  "an6.44:2.2": "My father Purāṇa was chaste, set apart, refraining from the vulgar act of sex. ",
  "an6.44:2.3": "When he passed away the Buddha declared that, since he was a once-returner, he was reborn in the host of joyful gods. ",
  "an6.44:2.4": "But my uncle Isidatta was not chaste; he lived content with his wife. ",
  "an6.44:2.5": "When he passed away the Buddha declared that, since he too was a once-returner, he was reborn in the host of joyful gods. ",
  "an6.44:2.6": "How on earth are we supposed to understand the teaching taught by the Buddha, when the chaste and the unchaste are both reborn in exactly the same place in the next life?” ",
  "an6.44:2.7": "“You’re right, sister, but that’s how the Buddha declared it.” ",
  "an6.44:3.1": "Then Ānanda, after receiving almsfood at Migasālā’s home, rose from his seat and left. ",
